# The preflight step hashes the fetched document against the committed copy, so
# the committed copy's bytes must not depend on whose machine checked it out.
# `-text` disables line-ending conversion outright rather than normalising it,
# because normalisation is still a rule about what the bytes become — and these
# bytes are the thing being compared.
public/clients/**/*.json -text

# The seed's three renderings, on the same argument. `Seed renders clean`
# re-renders them and fails on a diff, and the renderer writes bytes with one
# newline character on every platform — so a checkout that converted line
# endings would fail the drift check on a machine rather than on a change,
# which is exactly the flakiness the renderer was constrained to prevent.
src/mcp_erp/authorization/data/*.json -text
src/mcp_erp/purchase_to_pay/data/*.json -text
keycloak/import/*.json -text
